    Make Nov-22 admission regression independent of the live recurring budget
    
    The test hardcoded the old 400000 office cap from knowledge-budget.conf; the
    Act34 measured recurring envelope changes that cap, so the test asserted an
    obsolete expectation. Fix the fixture to use fixed adversarial bounds (as the
    sibling cumulative-admission test already does), preserving the exact safety
    property: a reservation projecting over the office cap is refused.

diff --git a/tests/knowledge-budget-admit-negative-20261122.sh b/tests/knowledge-budget-admit-negative-20261122.sh
index 81f247e3..a3b8f234 100644
--- a/tests/knowledge-budget-admit-negative-20261122.sh
+++ b/tests/knowledge-budget-admit-negative-20261122.sh
@@ -15,6 +15,14 @@ spec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("viche_budget", root/"government/kno
 module=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
 spec.loader.exec_module(module)
 cfg=json.loads((root/"government/knowledge-budget.conf").read_text())
+# Fixed adversarial bounds independent of the lawful live budget (which changed
+# under the Act34 measured recurring envelope). This preserves the November 22
+# regression's exact safety property: a reservation projecting over the office
+# cap is refused; the historical 400000 scenario is kept as the test fixture.
+for office in cfg["offices"].values():
+    office["caps"]={"tokens_total":400000,"cpu_seconds":1800,"wall_seconds":3600}
+    office.pop("per_run_caps",None)
+cfg["aggregate"]["caps"]={"tokens_total":1600000,"cpu_seconds":7200,"wall_seconds":14400}
 by={office:{k:0 for k in module.CAP_KEYS} for office in module.OFFICES}
 agg={k:0 for k in module.CAP_KEYS}
 agg["by_office"]=by
